  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Indonesia Partnership for Justice Phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Indonesia Partnership for Justice Phase 2 (AIPJ2) supports cooperation between the Governments of Australia and Indonesia on law, justice and security. It is designed to respond flexibly to the priorities of both governments. AIPJ2 focuses on leveraging Indonesia&#x2019;s resources to support policy reforms in the criminal justice system (e.g. courts and corrections); preventing violent extremism and transnational crime; and strengthening human rights including gender equality and disability inclusion. AIPJ2 works with a range of Indonesian government agencies and civil society organisations, as well as relevant Australian government agencies.</narrative>
  </description>
